 "caveats": [
  "sale_eur_m2 is a spliced series: 2016-2018 from INE Metodologia 2018 (0010033, NUTS 2013 geography) and 2019-2025 from INE Metodologia 2022 (0012255, NUTS 2024 geography). Where both exist (2019, 2020) they differ: Lisboa 3247 vs 3286 (2019) and 3377 vs 3415 (2020); some parishes differ more (e.g. Santa Maria Maior 2020: 5914 vs 5682; Misericórdia 2019: 4813 vs 4933). Raw series from both methodologies are kept in raw_series.",
  "rent_eur_m2 is a spliced series: 2017-2019 from INE Metodologia 2021 (0009631) and 2020-2025 from INE Metodologia 2026 (0014698). In the 2020-2023 overlap the two differ slightly (Lisboa 2023: 15.22 vs 15.38). 2016 is null because INE local rent statistics start in 2017. Raw series in raw_series.",
  "All INE local price values are medians over the full calendar year (= 12 months ending Q4), computed by INE from tax (IMT/AT) data for sales and from lease contracts declared to the Tax Authority for rents (new leases only). They are transaction medians, not asking prices; parish medians can be volatile year to year, likely due to composition effects (e.g. Marvila sale median jumps from 3335 in 2021 to 5440 in 2022; Santa Maria Maior moves 5682 -> 4157 between 2020 and 2021).",
  "2026 is null in both annual price series because INE has not published full-year 2026 data. The latest rolling values are given separately: sale_eur_m2_12m_to_2026Q1 (Apr 2025-Mar 2026) and rent_eur_m2_12m_to_2026Q2 (Jul 2025-Jun 2026).",
  "Sale values are for \"alojamentos familiares\" total (houses + apartments, new + existing; category H1). Rent values are for all new lease contracts of family dwellings.",
  "construction_cost_index is the national (Portugal) index, base 2021=100, annual mean of monthly values; it is not Lisbon-specific. 2026 is partial (Jan-Aug) and given separately in construction_cost_index_2026_ytd.",
  "euribor_12m_avg uses ECB annual averages of daily observations (2015-2025). 2026 is partial (Jan-Sep 2026 mean of monthly averages) and given separately in euribor_12m_avg_2026_ytd. euribor_6m_avg added as extra.",
  "AL registrations are a snapshot of the RNAL web service on 2026-10-10 (after Lisbon cancelled ~6,765 registrations in 2026 for missing insurance proof, so counts are far lower than the ~19-20k of 2023-2025). Parish attribution uses the register's own DTMNFR field.",
  "al.ratio_pct is COMPUTED here (not published by CML): RNAL registrations / INE Census 2021 alojamentos familiares clássicos (total) x 100, which follows the RMAL definition of the ratio. CML monitors and publishes the ratio monthly; its figures cited at approval (late 2025, pre-cancellation) are in cml_ratio_pct_cited_dec2025 for the 6 parishes named in the PLMJ note (e.g. Santa Maria Maior 66.9% vs 40.8% computed now). The CML monthly table itself could not be retrieved (dados.cm-lisboa.pt / dadosabertos.cm-lisboa.pt blocked by a Cloudflare challenge).",
  "Parish codes: INE uses NUTS-prefixed geocodes (1701106xx in NUTS 2013 series, 1A01106xx in NUTS 2024 series); they have been normalised here to the 6-digit DICOFRE codes given (and 1106 for the municipality). the same 24 Lisbon parish codes (post-2012 reform) appear in every series used."
 ],
